#version 460

// 05 SAMPLE MEDIUM INTERACTION - NOT IMPLEMENTED. Stub.
//
// This kernel is a placeholder so that every box of the PBR wavefront figure has a file on
// disk. The renderer has no participating media, so src/rt_kernels.cpp registers this variant
// with `implemented = false`: the scheduler never dispatches it and the Raytracer Shaders panel
// shows the slot greyed out. Deleting the body below and filling it in, then flipping that one
// flag, is what turns it on.
//
// WHAT IT WOULD DO. For each path whose ray passes through a medium, sample a distance along
// the ray against the medium's majorant. If the sampled point is closer than the surface hit
// that kernel 02 recorded, the path scatters in the volume: push it onto a medium-scatter queue
// for kernel 07 and cancel its surface interaction. Otherwise it reaches the surface, and the
// path is passed through to the same classification queues 02 already uses, with its throughput
// scaled by the transmittance along the way.
//
// See docs/plans/participating-media.md for the plan, including which queues and buffers it
// adds and where they hook into the kernel registry.

#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require
